\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Away With Our Sorrow And Fear!
\par We soon shall recover our home,
\par The city of saints shall appear,
\par The day of eternity come:
\par From earth we shall quickly remove,
\par And mount to our native abode,
\par The house of our Father above,
\par The palace of angels and God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our mourning is all at an end,
\par When, raised by the life- giving word,
\par We see the new city descend;
\par Adorned as a bride for her Lord;
\par The city so holy and clean,
\par No sorrow can breathe in the air,
\par No gloom of affliction or sin,
\par No shadow of evil is there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. By faith we already behold
\par That lovely Jerusalem here;
\par Her walls are of jasper and gold;
\par As crystal her buildings are clear;
\par Immovably founded in grace,
\par She stands as she ever hath stood,
\par And brightly her Builder displays,
\par And flames with the glory of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. No need of the sun in that day,
\par Which never is followed by night,
\par Where Jesus's beauties display
\par A pure and a permanent light:
\par The Lamb is their light and their sun,
\par And lo, by reflection they shine,
\par With Jesus ineffably one,
\par And bright in effulgence divine.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

